WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.934
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.069
is an Emmy Award-winning actress
and comedian

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.237
you know from her work
in "Girls Trip"

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.338
and "The Last O.G."

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:08.274
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.777
our very good friend
Tiffany Haddish.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.812
Tiffany, I am always so happy
to see you.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.280
You are such a positive person.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.349
I believe you to be an
optimistic person.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.650
You're a very funny person.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.186
It must be so difficult
for you to find the way

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.955
to talk about this moment
that we're living through.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.891
-It's extremely difficult.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.694
You know, Seth,
I like to think of myself

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.529
as an administrator of joys --
someone who

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:32.198
when I come into a scene,

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.867
any worries or woes
that you might have

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.769
can be alleviated or removed.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:40.606
But during this time,
it has been so difficult

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.542
for me to express
any kind of joy

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:48.147
or bring any kind of happiness
or anything 'cause it's --

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:52.252
'cause I'm watching --
I'm literally sitting back,

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:56.522
watching the world fall apart --
what it feels like.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.424
And it feels like
it needs to fall apart.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:00.893
Things need to fall apart
and be put back together again

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:04.563
in a way that's fair.

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:10.403
-You, uh -- You were at George
Floyd's funeral in Minneapolis,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.840
and what was it like
being there?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.042
What made you decide to go?

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.745
Were you happy, in the end,
that you went?

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:22.949
-I -- Okay, so, I decided to go
because I was invited.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.117
Right?
I was invited to be there.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:29.755
Um...and the main thing that
made me want to be there --

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.591
Mind you, I ain't been nowhere,
okay?

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.125
[ Chuckles ] In months.

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.727
But the thing that made me
really want to be there

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:39.465
is I have watched my friends
be slaughtered by the police.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.801
I have watched people be
murdered in front of me

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:47.006
as a 13-year-old, 14-year-old
girl, you know?

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.942
And there was nothing I can do
except "No! Don't do that!"

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:52.845
Yelling out?
What did that do? Like...

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.747
And so I wanted to be there
in support of the family

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.583
because I understand
how they feel,

00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:00.253
and being there was like...

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.687
being there for all my friends

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.422
whose funerals
I already went to.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.491
But all my friends
who passed away,

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.594
all the people that I went to
school with who've passed away,

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.030
have been locked up
for no reason,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.532
just 'cause they can't afford
a good lawyer

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.969
or, you know, accused of things
that they didn't do.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:18.037
And being there was so powerful,

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:21.206
'cause I did not know
it was gonna be televised.

00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:23.042
I had no idea that it
was gonna be televised.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.478
I thought there would be cameras
outside or whatever.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.881
But that was my first time
walking into a funeral

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:32.551
that was televised and a funeral
of someone who was being --

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:35.154
who was killed
by a police officer.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:36.288
You know?

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.424
And I thought that
was really tremendous.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.360
And I -- I remember I was like,
"Kevin, put your mask on.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.427
Y'all need to put your mask on."

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.795
Nobody wanted
to put their mask on.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.129
I don't know why.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:45.498
But I'm "Put your mask on
if you're sitting next to me."

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.532
They didn't want to put it on.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.967
But Will Packer put his on.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.437
And, you know, the serv--
the eulogies that were given

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.905
were so powerful.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.807
It was a great message.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:58.344
And I cried so much.
I cried so much.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:01.614
I was crying so much,
and it was like tears of

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:05.318
not just for Floyd but for --
for all of those people

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:09.422
that passed away and all of my
friends and my family members

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.789
that are locked up

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:14.060
and, like, it was just like
all the tears that

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.729
I ever wanted to cry
were coming up,

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:20.667
and I was trying to swallow
them, trying to swallow them.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.803
When they had that moment
of silence --

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:28.140
that 8 minutes and 46 seconds
of silence on that stage...

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.945
And I'm standing there next to
one of the mothers of a victim,

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.782
and I'm -- the quietness
and then the thought of

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:40.886
what if someone's knee
was in my neck for this long?

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.156
[ Voice breaking ]
How helpless were my friends

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:47.026
when they were being attacked,
you know?

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:50.195
I just couldn't -- the tears --
I was trying to swallow them

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:51.530
and they was coming out
through my nose

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.367
and my mask was full of snot.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.168
And I was, like, holding it,

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:59.071
trying to, like,
keep the snot off my mouth.

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.539
But ain't no holding it.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:02.007
And I wasn't gonna take it off

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:04.911
'cause I didn't want to look
like a scene out of a bad movie.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.646
And I just --
The pain --

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:12.050
The amount of pain that I felt
was tremendous.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.286
And -- And as we're leaving out
of there and I --

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:15.488
You know, people are like,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.256
"Oh, they already Tweeting
about you.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.858
They already Tweeting
about you."

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.626
And I'm like,
"I didn't do anything!"

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:25.365
I didn't do anything and already
being, like, attacked.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.632
And I'm like, "It's not about --

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.434
I don't care if they're Tweeting
about me."

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.902
If they're Tweeting about me

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.838
and that's bringing
more attention

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.873
to what's going on right now,
great.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.242
But when I took that mask off

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:40.847
and all that snot
was all over in here,

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.114
that was not okay.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.583
But the next day, my skin
was so soft all from here,

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.886
so I found out
about snot facials.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.355
-There you go.
So, uh...

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.759
there's at least one
very tiny, tiny positive.

